---
title: About
layout: layouts/base.njk
---
<h1>About</h1>

<details class="about-section" data-section="me">
  <summary><h2>Me</h2></summary>
  <p>I am a front-end engineer who builds applications and components using JavaScript, HTML, and CSS. I love building cool things, especially using JavaScript. I have worked on small and large code bases and enjoy the unique challenges presented by both — today as a Senior Staff Frontend Engineer at Pendo.io.</p>

  {# Strava Widget (see CONTEXT.md) — placement/visual design here are
     deliberately minimal, not polished: guntherjh/guntherjh.github.io#24's
     map explicitly deferred widget visual design/placement as a follow-on
     effort once the data contract existed; this just gets it on the page.
     Guarded with {% if strava %} since src/_data/strava.json doesn't exist
     until the Refresh Job's first run completes — an Eleventy global data
     file is optional, so referencing an absent one is safe, not a build
     error. #}
  {% if strava %}
  <div class="strava-widget">
    <h3>Recent Activities</h3>
    <ul class="strava-activities">
      {% for activity in strava.activities %}
      <li>
        <strong>{{ activity.type }}</strong> — {{ activity.name }} —
        {{ activity.distance | metersToMiles | round(1) }} mi,
        {{ (activity.moving_time / 60) | round }} min
        — <time datetime="{{ activity.start_date }}">{{ activity.start_date | readableDate }}</time>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>

    <h3>Recent Stats <span class="strava-stats-window">(last 4 weeks)</span></h3>
    <ul class="strava-stats">
      {% for sport, totals in strava.stats %}
      <li>
        <strong>{{ sport }}</strong>:
        {{ totals.count }} {{ "activity" if totals.count == 1 else "activities" }},
        {{ totals.distance | metersToMiles | round(1) }} mi
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>

    <p class="strava-updated">Last updated {{ strava.capturedAt | readableDate }}</p>
  </div>
  {% else %}
  <p class="strava-widget-pending">Strava activity data will appear here once the Refresh Job's first run completes.</p>
  {% endif %}
</details>

<details class="about-section" data-section="site">
  <summary><h2>This site</h2></summary>
  <p>Work in progress.</p>

  {# Latest run plus the one before it (may not exist yet — e.g. right
     after guntherjh/guntherjh.github.io#71's Snapshot-shape migration, or
     before the second-ever audit) for the trend indicators below. See
     ADR 0006 for why the Snapshot retains history at all. #}
  {% set latest = lighthouse.history[0] %}
  {% set previous = lighthouse.history[1] %}
  {% set previousDate = (previous.capturedAt | readableDate) if previous else none %}
  {% set metricNames = {
    "performance": "Performance", "accessibility": "Accessibility",
    "best-practices": "Best Practices", "seo": "SEO",
    "lcp": "LCP", "cls": "CLS", "tbt": "TBT"
  } %}
  {# Renders one metric value the way its column wants it — LCP in seconds,
     TBT in whole ms, everything else (0-100 scores, unitless CLS) bare.
     One macro so the cell text and the trend toggletip's copy can't drift. #}
  {% macro fmtMetric(key, value) -%}
    {%- if key == "lcp" -%}{{ (value / 1000) | round(1) }}s
    {%- elif key == "tbt" -%}{{ value | round }}ms
    {%- else -%}{{ value }}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endmacro -%}
  {# Trend marker for one cell. An actual tier change (improved/regressed)
     is a native-Popover toggletip button (see ADR 0007); a flat arrow is
     plain text; no previous run means no marker at all. #}
  {% macro trendMarker(change, detailId, ariaLabel, detail) -%}
    {%- if change and change.outcome != "flat" -%}
      <button type="button" class="lh-trend lh-trend-{{ change.outcome }}" popovertarget="{{ detailId }}" aria-label="{{ ariaLabel }}" aria-describedby="{{ detailId }}">{{ "↑" if change.direction == "up" else "↓" }}</button><span popover id="{{ detailId }}" class="lh-trend-detail">{{ detail }}</span>
    {%- elif change -%}
      <span class="lh-trend lh-trend-flat" aria-label="No tier change since previous audit">–</span>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endmacro -%}
  <div class="lighthouse-widget">
    {# Only the table scrolls sideways on a narrow screen (see #41); the
       legend and glossary below stay outside the scroll wrapper so a
       horizontal scrollbar can't drag a vertical one in with it (#124). #}
    <div class="lighthouse-table-scroll">
      <table>
        <caption>
          Lighthouse scores, last measured {{ latest.capturedAt | readableDate }}
          {%- if previous %}
          — trend vs. previous audit ({{ previousDate }})
          {%- endif %}
        </caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Page</th>
            <th scope="col" abbr="Performance" aria-describedby="lh-def-performance">Perf</th>
            <th scope="col" abbr="Accessibility" aria-describedby="lh-def-accessibility">A11y</th>
            <th scope="col" abbr="Best Practices" aria-describedby="lh-def-best-practices">BP</th>
            <th scope="col" aria-describedby="lh-def-seo">SEO</th>
            <th scope="col" abbr="Largest Contentful Paint" aria-describedby="lh-def-lcp">LCP</th>
            <th scope="col" abbr="Cumulative Layout Shift" aria-describedby="lh-def-cls">CLS</th>
            <th scope="col" abbr="Total Blocking Time" aria-describedby="lh-def-tbt">TBT</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for label, page in latest.pages %}
          {% set prevPage = previous.pages[label] if previous else none %}
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">{{ label }}</th>
            {% for key in ["performance", "accessibility", "best-practices", "seo"] %}
            {% set value = page.scores[key] %}
            {% set prevValue = prevPage.scores[key] if prevPage else none %}
            {% set level = value | scoreLevel %}
            {% set prevLevel = (prevValue | scoreLevel) if prevPage else none %}
            {% set change = level | trend(prevLevel) %}
            {% set detailId = "lh-trend-" ~ (label | lower | replace(" ", "-")) ~ "-" ~ key %}
            {% set ariaLabel = (metricNames[key] ~ " " ~ change.outcome ~ " since previous audit") if change else "" %}
            {% set detail = {
              label: metricNames[key], currentDisplay: value, currentLevel: level,
              previousDisplay: prevValue, previousLevel: prevLevel, previousDate: previousDate
            } | trendDetail %}
            <td class="lh-cell lh-{{ level }}" data-label="{{ metricNames[key] }}">{{ value }} {{ trendMarker(change, detailId, ariaLabel, detail) }}</td>
            {% endfor %}
            {% for key in ["lcp", "cls", "tbt"] %}
            {% set value = page[key] %}
            {% set prevValue = prevPage[key] if prevPage else none %}
            {% set level = value | metricLevel(key) %}
            {% set prevLevel = (prevValue | metricLevel(key)) if prevPage else none %}
            {% set change = level | trend(prevLevel) %}
            {% set detailId = "lh-trend-" ~ (label | lower | replace(" ", "-")) ~ "-" ~ key %}
            {% set ariaLabel = (metricNames[key] ~ " " ~ change.outcome ~ " since previous audit") if change else "" %}
            {% set detail = {
              label: metricNames[key], currentDisplay: fmtMetric(key, value) | trim, currentLevel: level,
              previousDisplay: (fmtMetric(key, prevValue) | trim) if prevValue is not none else none,
              previousLevel: prevLevel, previousDate: previousDate
            } | trendDetail %}
            <td class="lh-cell lh-{{ level }}" data-label="{{ metricNames[key] }}">{{ fmtMetric(key, value) }} {{ trendMarker(change, detailId, ariaLabel, detail) }}</td>
            {% endfor %}
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="lighthouse-legend">
      Green = good, orange = needs improvement, red = poor, per Lighthouse's own thresholds.
      <span class="lighthouse-legend-trend">↑ ↓ – show whether a score's tier improved, regressed, or held since the previous audit — activate ↑ or ↓ for the earlier value.</span>
    </p>
    <details class="lighthouse-glossary">
      <summary>What do these metrics mean?</summary>
      <dl>
        <div>
          <dt>Perf — Performance</dt>
          <dd id="lh-def-performance">Lighthouse's weighted score (0–100) combining lab metrics — weighted most heavily toward LCP, TBT and CLS. ≥ 90 good, 50–89 needs improvement, &lt; 50 poor.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>A11y — Accessibility</dt>
          <dd id="lh-def-accessibility">Weighted pass/fail automated accessibility checks (Lighthouse runs axe-core). Same 0–100 banding. A perfect score still needs manual testing to confirm — automated checks can't catch everything.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>BP — Best Practices</dt>
          <dd id="lh-def-best-practices">Equally-weighted general web-quality and security checks — HTTPS, no console errors, no deprecated APIs, correct image aspect ratios, a Content Security Policy. Same 0–100 banding.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>SEO</dt>
          <dd id="lh-def-seo">Basic technical-SEO checks — page is crawlable, has a title and meta description, returns a successful status, uses descriptive link text and a valid canonical. Fundamentals only, not a full SEO audit. Same 0–100 banding.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>LCP — Largest Contentful Paint</dt>
          <dd id="lh-def-lcp">Time until the largest image or text block in the viewport renders. Good ≤ 2.5 s, poor &gt; 4 s.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>CLS — Cumulative Layout Shift</dt>
          <dd id="lh-def-cls">How much visible content shifts position unexpectedly while the page loads (unitless). Good ≤ 0.1, poor &gt; 0.25.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>TBT — Total Blocking Time</dt>
          <dd id="lh-def-tbt">Total time the main thread was blocked by long tasks during load, delaying response to input. Good ≤ 200 ms, poor &gt; 600 ms.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </details>
  </div>
</details>

